      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "75 patients have been given prostaglandin inhibitor dicloberl in a complex therapy. Comparative analysis of traditionally treated patients with renal stones and with dicloberl in a complex therapy is presented in the article. The combination of dicloberl with tramadol was found to be more effective drug treatment for patients with renal colic. This treatment has to be applied for patients with renal stones up to 6 mm. It is an effective pharmacotherapy for excreting renal stones."},
